-- Migration 0037_matter_graph_foundations: generated by drizzle-kit (types, tables, keys), enum rename, RLS, function and triggers hand-written, reviewed before commit.
-- Reviewed-by: Claude (agent, #344)
-- Matter-graph foundations (#344, part 1 of #32; ADR 0013):
--   * confirmation_state is redefined as proposed|confirmed|auto_applied|corrected. No column uses
--     the type yet, so drizzle-kit's DROP/CREATE TYPE is replaced by two RENAME VALUEs (same labels
--     in the same order, nothing dropped). provenance() also gains captured_at; both apply to the
--     fact tables of the later parts.
--   * The #32 enums (forum side, jurisdiction kind, adapter level, bench kind, proceeding kind and
--     state, list type, appearance capacity, order type, obligation source and status, person kind,
--     role edge kind, document kind and text status) for the later parts.
--   * forum, court_hall, bench: global-or-workspace reference tables. A null workspace_id is the
--     system catalogue (owner-written via owner_catalogue, readable by every workspace via
--     global_read); a workspace id is a custom row under ws_isolation. The app role cannot write a
--     null-workspace row (ws_isolation's WITH CHECK fails on null). forum.code is unique per scope
--     (NULLS NOT DISTINCT). Grants come from the default privileges (app: 02-roles.sql, clerk: 0022).
--   * app_reference_scope_guard(ref_table, fk_column, mode): BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE trigger function
--     for single-column FKs into a global-or-workspace table. It runs as the invoker, so the lookup
--     only sees rows visible under RLS, and rejects (23503) a reference that is missing, invisible
--     or, in mode `same`, of another scope (`same_or_global` also accepts a catalogue row). The
--     error is the same in every case, so it is no existence oracle. court_hall and bench use `same`.
--   * member (workspace_id, id) unique key: target for the composite member FKs of later parts.
-- Expand only: nothing existing is dropped; member gains a constraint.
